# UI style: the Settings look, everywhere

The Settings screens are the reference for how BluePLM looks: quiet, typographic, flat, and Claude-like.
Every new or reworked screen (panes, views, dialogs, menus, toasts) looks the same way and is built
from the same parts. Set by the user on 2026-11-04 ("really good standardized UI design for
aesthetics ... reflect the beautiful UI style of the settings").

## Build from the primitives

Import from `@/components/core/ui`. Never hand-roll a control that a primitive already provides.

| Need | Use |
|---|---|
| Page or pane body | `Page` (sections 40px apart; `gap="tight"` 24px in panes) |
| A titled part | `Section` (`title`, `description`, `actions`; `density="compact"` in narrow panes) |
| Rows with hairlines between | `RowGroup` holding `Row` (setting: label + sentence left, control right) or `ListRow` (selectable two-line item) |
| Side pane title bar | `PaneHeader` (44px, title, count, IconButtons, hairline below) |
| Buttons | `Button` (`primary` once per view, `secondary` for the rest, `ghost` in toolbars, `danger` / `danger-subtle` for destructive), `IconButton` for icon-only, `OverflowMenu` for "more" |
| Toolbars | `ActionBar` |
| Inputs | `TextInput`, `TextArea`, `Select`, `Switch`, `SegmentedControl` (the shared `FIELD_CLASS` look) |
| States in words | `StatusText` (tone + 12px glyph, never colour alone). `Badge` only for a count or a label that must stand out (Admin, Overdue) |
| Messages in a page | `Callout` |
| Empty, error, signed-out | `EmptyState` (a line, a sentence, buttons; no illustration) |
| Menus | `MenuPanel` + `MenuItem` |

If a screen needs a part that does not exist yet, add it to `src/components/core/ui/`, with its JSDoc,
once. Never style it locally in a feature. Settings re-exports these under its own names, so the two
can never drift.

## Tokens

- **Colour: `ui-*` only** (`bg-ui-bg`, `bg-ui-nav`, `bg-ui-field`, `bg-ui-hover`, `bg-ui-selected`,
  `border-ui-border`, `divide-ui-divider`, `text-ui-fg`, `text-ui-fg-secondary`, `text-ui-fg-tertiary`,
  `ui-accent`, `ui-danger`, `ui-success`, `ui-warning`).
  - They are CSS variables in `src/index.css` with dark and light values, so a screen built on them
    themes itself.
  - Never a raw hex or a Tailwind palette colour (`gray-700`, `blue-500`).
  - Do not use the legacy `plm-*` tokens in new UI. Replace them when reworking a screen.
- **Type:** `font-ui` (system UI stack) with these sizes:
  - 16px semibold: section and dialog titles
  - 14px: body, row labels and list titles
  - 13px: secondary lines, descriptions in panes and table cells
  - 12px: badges, keycaps and tiny meta

  Use weight 400 / 500 / 600, nothing heavier. Line heights: 20px for single lines, 1.4 for prose.
  Use `tabular-nums` for numbers that line up.
- **Hierarchy from type size and grey level, not boxes.**
  - No cards around sections, and no fills behind groups. Use hairlines (`divide-ui-divider`)
    between rows and `border-ui-border` between regions.
  - A shadow only on floating layers (menus, dialogs, popovers).
- **Spacing:** sections 40px apart (24px in panes); row padding 16px (10px compact). Pages have a 16px
  gutter (`px-4`) and a readable max width for forms. Side navigation is 256px on `bg-ui-nav`.
- **Shape:**
  - `rounded-lg` (8px) on buttons, fields, menu items and rounded list rows
  - `rounded-xl` on dialogs and floating windows
  - `rounded-md` on badges and keycaps
- **Icons:** lucide.
  - 14px in buttons, 16px in rows and toolbars, 18px with `strokeWidth={1.6}` in navigation.
  - Icons are `text-ui-fg-secondary` unless they carry state.
  - Every icon-only button has a `title` and an `aria-label`.
- **Motion:** 100ms colour transitions (`transition-colors duration-100`) and `animate-dialog-in` for
  dialogs. Nothing bounces.
- **Focus:** `focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ui-accent/50`, as the primitives already do.
  Keyboard reachable everywhere.

## Writing on screen

- Sentence case everywhere ("Export order", not "Export Order"). Buttons are verbs.
- One primary action per view.
- Say what happened and what to do next. Never a raw error code or stack.
- Counts and states read as words: "3 files", "Missing STEP", "Sent 2 Nov".
- All text goes through `t()` (see CLAUDE.md).

## Layout patterns

- **Full-page module view** (Orders, Reviews, Settings): a list in a side pane (`PaneHeader` +
  search + `RowGroup` of `ListRow`), and the selection in the main area as a `Page` of `Section`s.
- **Tables:** 13px cells, a 12px `text-ui-fg-tertiary` header row and hairline row dividers. Row
  hover is `bg-ui-hover`, selection `bg-ui-selected`. No zebra stripes, no vertical rules.
  Right-align numbers. Row actions appear on hover (as `ListRow` does).
- **Dialogs:** `Dialog` / `ConfirmDialog` from `@/components/core/Dialog`, with a 16px title, a 14px
  sentence and buttons bottom-right (secondary Cancel, then primary). A destructive confirm uses
  `danger`.
- **Narrow and wide:** every pane works from 280px up. Text truncates with a `title`; nothing
  overflows horizontally.

## Checking it

Render it as `.cursor/rules/ui-look.mdc` says, then compare the screen side by side with a Settings
scene (`settings-*`). If it does not look like it belongs next to Settings, it is not done.
